  "summary": "Cold visual review of all three claude PDFs for pc-s51 (Twenty-fifth Sunday in Ordinary Time, Year A). Every page was inspected at full size from the build-artifacts-0000 rasters, whose review-cache pdf_sha256 values match the sealed receipts: study pc-s51-...-year-a.pdf sha256 fd3a4d13f7bb980bbe3bb6025dac194997add5bf40a9f53eb4bced31af81dcb8, pages 1-39 of 39; concise -synthesis.pdf sha256 09275d9d8d97c81068c262dc7cab16f24744ce9f1b0f1af9bce8fd39e2cfa96f, pages 1-12 of 12; homily -homily.pdf sha256 99a0877432a268bd56b92c4cfe45011d059a00ab42498113def2f376457bd70f, pages 1-6 of 6. Contact sheets were also opened. The three PDFs, the four pagination-evidence files and all 26 render inputs hash to the REVIEW_INPUTS seal. Mechanical checks: all fonts are embedded subsets (TeX Gyre Pagella X, LM Mono); the three logs have no overfull, underfull, undefined-reference or rerun warnings; text bounding boxes stay inside the margins on every page; TOC page numbers and running heads match the actual section starts. Study (39 pp, within 20-50): the title and contents page, the appointed-elements table with repeated header, three interpretations each opening on a fresh page and ending in its own four-sense list, the four-column comparison table, the Scriptural Date and Location dossier, the resolution and scope appendices and the References. Final page p39 carries the timestamp and compact rights colophon. Concise (12 pp, within 10-12): physical page 1 holds the complete 11-row map in liturgical order, with the Communion options labelled, then exactly four sense rows (Literal, Allegorical, Moral, Anagogical). Page 2 holds only the seven-unit Scriptural Date and Location dossier in canonical order. Pages 3-4 are two full pages of Themes and Movement. The Detailed Commentary begins on page 5 and interleaves the three readings and their witnesses by question. The settled zref markers (inventory, overview and senses on p1; chronology on p2; themes on p3-4; commentary on p5) agree with the pages. The appendix, References and colophon are on p10-12. Homily (6 pp): 13/18pt ragged-right speech on pp.1-4, with a blank line between paragraphs and a wider break between movements. The speech has no citations or directions in it. The Note on Sources and Delivery is on p5, and the References, timestamp and colophon are on p6. Limits: judged from pdftoppm rasters at 200 dpi plus text extraction; no print proof was made. Page-foot gaps at subsection and interpretation boundaries (study pp.10, 12, 18, 30, 32, 34; concise p.5) come from ragged-bottom breaks before headings and are acceptable. The one defect found is advisory. Verdict: PASS."
